From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:31:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Add a Firmware Update setup page

An update capsule can be staged only from an OS, and the setup shows
nothing of the system firmware: its version, the lowest version it
accepts, or how its last update went.

Add FirmwareUpdateDxe, built with CAPSULE_SUPPORT: a Platform Setup page
with the system firmware of the ESRT (the FMP instance of
PcdSystemFmpCapsuleImageTypeIdGuid) -- the BIOS version of SMBIOS, the
version, the lowest supported version, the last attempt version and
status -- read when the page opens.

"Update from a USB drive" checks \EFI\UpdateCapsule of the USB drives
and EFI system partitions, the places PlatformBootManagerLib reads:
exactly one file, an FMP capsule for this firmware, not older than the
lowest supported version. After a confirmation that names the versions
and the file, it sets EFI_OS_INDICATIONS_FILE_CAPSULE_DELIVERY_SUPPORTED
in OsIndications and restarts, so that the next boot applies the capsule
like one staged by an OS, signature check included. Nothing is written
here.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
